# ParaBank Selenium Automation Framework

A Selenium + TestNG + Maven test automation framework built against [ParaBank](https://parabank.parasoft.com), a live demo banking application. Built as a portfolio project demonstrating Page Object Model design, data-driven testing, failure reporting, and CI readiness.

## Tech Stack

- **Language:** Java 17
- **Build tool:** Maven
- **Test framework:** TestNG
- **Browser automation:** Selenium WebDriver 4
- **Driver management:** WebDriverManager (auto-resolves browser driver binaries)
- **Reporting:** ExtentReports (HTML report with screenshots on failure)
- **Logging:** Log4j2
- **CI:** GitHub Actions

## Features Tested

- User registration (positive + missing-field negative cases)
- Login (valid, invalid username, invalid password, empty fields)
- Accounts overview (page load, account listing)
- Open new account
- Fund transfer between accounts (valid, invalid amount, over-balance)
- Bill pay (valid payment, missing payee name)
- Find transactions (page navigation)

## Framework Architecture

```
src
├── main/java/com/parabank
│   ├── base/          → BaseTest: shared setup/teardown for every test class
│   ├── driver/         → DriverFactory: cross-browser driver creation (Chrome/Firefox/Edge)
│   ├── pages/          → Page Object classes (locators + actions, no assertions)
│   └── utilities/      → ConfigReader, WaitUtility, ScreenshotUtility, ExtentReportManager
│
└── test
    ├── java/com/parabank
    │   ├── tests/       → Test classes (@Test methods + assertions)
    │   └── listeners/   → TestListener: hooks into TestNG for reporting/screenshots
    └── resources
        ├── config/config.properties
        ├── testng.xml
        └── log4j2.xml
```

**Design principles applied:**
- Page Object Model — pages own locators/actions, tests own assertions
- No hardcoded values — browser/base URL externalized to `config.properties`
- No `Thread.sleep()` — all synchronization via `WebDriverWait` (explicit waits)
- ThreadLocal WebDriver — framework is parallel-execution safe out of the box
- TestNG groups (`smoke`, `sanity`, `regression`) for different execution needs

## Running the Tests

```bash
# Run the full suite (as defined in testng.xml)
mvn clean test

# Run only smoke tests
mvn clean test -Dgroups=smoke
```

Reports are generated at `reports/ExtentReport.html`. Failure screenshots are saved to `reports/screenshots/`. Logs are written to `reports/logs/automation.log`.

## Before You Run

The test data (`VALID_USERNAME` / `VALID_PASSWORD` constants and the placeholder account IDs in `TransferFundsTest`) needs to point to a real registered ParaBank test user, since ParaBank resets demo data periodically. Register a user via `RegistrationTest` or manually, then update those constants.

## TestNG Groups

| Group | Purpose | When to run |
|---|---|---|
| `smoke` | Critical happy-path checks | Every commit |
| `sanity` | Broader but still fast checks | Before merging a PR |
| `regression` | Full positive + negative coverage | Nightly / before release |

## CI/CD

A GitHub Actions workflow (`.github/workflows/ci.yml`) runs the Maven test suite in headless Chrome on every push/PR to `main`, and uploads the Extent report as a build artifact.

## Future Improvements

- Move test data (usernames, amounts, addresses) into external JSON/CSV files
- Add Fluent Wait for a couple of especially flaky elements
- Extend Find Transactions coverage once a stable seeded test account exists
